  "scope": "Shared bounded decoded XY retention for virtual desktop documents with persisted resource configuration in C++/Python and both ImGui launchers.",
  "semantics": "Window-owned creator-thread cache gives each frontend one current source/T/C/Z slot. Hits update recency; validated successful misses evict least-recently-used other slots. Weak registrations do not own closed frontends or providers. Eager tables bypass retention. Worker snapshots use independent caches with the captured budget. Caller-held shared images survive eviction. Staged cache slots publish only after successful document adoption; source values are copied before eviction and cache-source publication is statically checked nonallocating.",
  "limits": "viewport_cache_mb is a positive persisted Resources setting, default 128 MiB. The shared cache counts pixel-vector capacity, conservatively per retained slot. Shape admission rejects oversized XY before provider IO; excess returned vector capacity is rejected before retention. Shrinking settings immediately trims cache retention. Existing per-document decoded-view caps remain. Provider scratch/caches, outstanding caller handles, miss temporaries, allocator/metadata overhead, linked XYZ/readback/display buffers, GPU textures and process RSS are external. This is not a complete aggregate viewport memory bound.",
  "configuration": "The schema-generated ImGui preferences control and C++ Window.updateSettings / Python Editor.update_settings consume the same setting. Settings writes and invalid updates leave the cache intact on failure. Window.virtualViewCacheInfo / Editor.virtual_view_cache_info return detached creator-thread cache counters. New optional UI source is matched byte-for-byte to its installed facade during qualification.",
  "verification": "4422 selected Python checks per OS, including ten new cache/preferences checks and 35 settings regressions; ten native suites including the new cache suite, eight session groups, three desktop IO/startup/append regression suites, 36 rank-host cases / 499 checks and two resource groups per OS. Fresh installed SDK consumers verify the new setting and virtual TIFF API. Readers verify 144 existing reports / 27598 raw input frames; no new input cases are claimed. Native tests cover LRU/hits/misses, pre-read and actual-capacity admission, failed reads, immediate shrink, detached handles, weak-slot/provider lifetime, source identity, worker independence, failed document adoption and preference persistence. Python tests verify schema/defaults, detached diagnostics, strict and atomic invalid updates, actual ImGui control rendering and failed preference writes. No complete ImageJ/Fiji source/reference/resource/real-GPU/OS-desktop/platform acceptance.",
